[06/08/26 13:18:14] INFO     Transcription:  To find which element   base.py:98
                             appears at position n, we divide n by             
                             the cycle length and look at the                  
                             remainder. The remainder tells us                 
                             exactly where we are within the current           
                             cycle. A remainder of one points to the           
                             first element, a remainder of two to              
                             the second, and so on. If the remainder           
                             is zero, we have landed exactly on the            
                             last element of the cycle.                        
